# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cross-environment determinism golden file
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The committed golden file at `tools/benchmark/baselines/golden.json` contains
# ~11,000 hex-encoded Float64 reference values produced by the deterministic
# kernel generator. When the file is regenerated (rare event — Node major
# upgrade, deliberate kernel optimisation, accepted drift), the resulting diff
# spans every line; a line-by-line text diff is unreviewable and offers no
# semantic value to reviewers.
#
# Marking the file with the `binary` macro (which unsets `diff`, `merge`, and
# `text`) makes `git diff` and PR review interfaces display "Binary files
# differ" instead of a multi-megabyte line-by-line diff. Reviewers focus on
# the PR description (regeneration trigger + new state hash) and rely on the
# CI smoke step to verify the regenerated file matches the current kernel
# output. See `packages/math2d/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md` ADR-018 and
# `tools/benchmark/README.md` for the regeneration flow.
tools/benchmark/baselines/golden.json binary
